### 2. CORE OBJECTIVE

Build a centralized, privacy-aware student data management, admission reconciliation, regulatory monitoring and academic record verification platform for AICTE-approved institutions.

The platform must allow institutions to submit and update student-level enrolment data using APAAR ID as the proposed primary academic identifier. It must validate incoming records, detect potential duplicates, compare enrolment against applicable approved intake, maintain admission timelines, manage discrepancies, provide evidence-backed alerts, offer AICTE monitoring dashboards and support controlled verification of academic credentials.

The application must implement the following end-to-end workflow:

Institution registration and authentication
→ approved intake configuration
→ student data upload or secure API submission
→ schema normalization
→ record validation
→ APAAR-related identifier checks
→ cross-institution reconciliation
→ intake and category validation
→ discrepancy investigation and correction
→ authorized approval
→ central student record repository
→ AICTE analytics and monitoring
→ controlled academic credential verification
→ regulatory reports and auditable records.

The platform must also demonstrate innovative capabilities beyond a conventional student management dashboard.

